      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems too complicated that I don\u0027t understand. Why not just use `poll` to read exactly the given number of bytes?\n\n```\nint read_exact(int fd, uint8_t *buf, size_t count, int timeout_ms) {\n    size_t total_read \u003d 0;\n    while (total_read \u003c count) {\n        struct pollfd pfd \u003d { .fd \u003d fd, .events \u003d POLLIN };\n        int ret \u003d poll(\u0026pfd, 1, timeout_ms);\n\n        if (ret \u003c 0) {\n            perror(\"poll failed\");\n            return -1;\n        }\n        if (ret \u003d\u003d 0) {\n            fprintf(stderr, \"Read timed out\\n\");\n            return -1;\n        }\n\n        ssize_t bytes_read \u003d read(fd, buf + total_read, count - total_read);\n        if (bytes_read \u003c 0) {\n            perror(\"read failed\");\n            return -1;\n        }\n        if (bytes_read \u003d\u003d 0) { // Should not happen after successful poll\n            fprintf(stderr, \"Read returned 0 (EOF?)\\n\");\n            return -1;\n        }\n        total_read +\u003d bytes_read;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
